IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `taa-types`
IMPORT `taa-dates`

-- Tax Administration Act 1994 — GOALS 3 AND 4: LATE FILING, LATE PAYMENT AND
-- SHORTFALL PENALTIES.
--
--   "What late filing penalty applies; what late payment penalty has accrued
--    on unpaid tax by a date; and what shortfall penalty applies?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1994_166.txt — ss 139A,
-- 139B, 141A-141K, 141JAA.

§ `Goal 3 — late filing and late payment`

-- s 139A "(3) The late filing penalty for an annual tax return for a taxpayer
-- with net income— (a) below $100,000, is $50; (b) between $100,000 and
-- $1,000,000 (both figures inclusive), is $250; (c) above $1,000,000, is $500.
-- (3B) The late filing penalty for a multinational top-up tax return is $500.
-- (4) The late filing penalty for an annual ICA return or reconciliation
-- statement or employment income information or statement for RLWT is $250."
-- (2): only if the return is not provided on time "and the Commissioner
-- notifies the taxpayer that the penalty is payable".
@ref s 139A(2)-(4)
@export The late filing penalty under s 139A of the Tax Administration Act 1994 (NZ): for a late annual tax return, $50 for net income below $100,000, $250 from $100,000 to $1,000,000, and $500 above; $500 for a multinational top-up tax return; $250 for an ICA return, reconciliation statement, employment income information or RLWT statement — only once the Commissioner has notified that the penalty is payable. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of return`  @desc The kind of return
      net IS A NUMBER  @desc The taxpayer's net income (for an annual tax return)
      late IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the return was not provided on time
      notified IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the Commissioner has notified the taxpayer that the penalty is payable
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the late filing penalty for` k `, net income` net `, late` late `, notified` notified MEANS
    IF   NOT (late AND notified)
    THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER k
         WHEN `an annual tax return` THEN
             BRANCH
                 IF net LESS THAN 100000 THEN 50
                 IF net AT MOST 1000000 THEN 250
                 OTHERWISE 500
         WHEN `a multinational top-up tax return` THEN 500
         WHEN `an annual ICA return, reconciliation statement, employment income information or RLWT statement` THEN 250

-- s 139B "(1) This section applies to a taxpayer if ... the taxpayer does not
-- pay by the default date an amount of tax ..., and— (a) the unpaid tax is
-- provisional tax or a penalty relating to a failure to pay provisional tax:
-- (b) ... the Commissioner determines that the taxpayer has failed to pay on
-- time an amount of tax due ... in the period ... 2 years before the default
-- date ...: (c) ... the Commissioner determines that the taxpayer has paid on
-- time ... and— (i) the Commissioner gives the taxpayer a notice setting a
-- further date for payment ...; and (ii) the taxpayer does not pay the unpaid
-- tax before the date that is the earlier of the further date and the date
-- that is 1 month after the date of the notice."
@ref s 139B(1)
GIVEN p IS A `Late payment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 139B applies to` p IF
        unpaidAfter (p's `default date`)
    AND (    p's `provisional tax or a penalty for not paying it`
         OR  p's `paid late in the 2 years before the default date`
         OR  (CONSIDER p's `notice of a further date given on`
              WHEN JUST notice THEN
                  CONSIDER p's `further date for payment`
                  WHEN JUST further THEN
                      CONSIDER p's `tax paid on`
                      WHEN JUST paid THEN paid AT LEAST earlier further (`add months` notice 1)
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
              WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE))
    WHERE
        GIVEN d IS A DATE
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        unpaidAfter d MEANS
            CONSIDER p's `tax paid on`
            WHEN JUST paid THEN paid GREATER THAN d
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        GIVEN x IS A DATE, y IS A DATE
        GIVETH A DATE
        earlier x y MEANS IF x LESS THAN y THEN x ELSE y

-- s 139B "(2) The taxpayer is liable to pay a late payment penalty consisting
-- of— (a) an initial late payment penalty equal to the total of— (i) 1% of
-- the unpaid tax; and (ii) 4% of the amount of tax to pay at the end of the
-- sixth day after the day on which a penalty under subparagraph (i) is
-- imposed; and (b) an incremental late payment penalty equal to 1% of the
-- amount of tax to pay determined on each day that falls 1 month after a day
-- on which a penalty is imposed under— (i) this subsection". (3) "(a) [the
-- 1% is added] on the day after the default date ...: (b) [the 4% is added]
-- at the end of the sixth day after the day referred to in paragraph (a)."
-- (4) "An incremental late payment penalty is to be added ... on the day
-- after the last day of successive monthly intervals during which the tax to
-- pay remains unpaid." "Tax to pay" includes penalties already imposed. The
-- monthly intervals run from the day after the default date (fork F3); a
-- payment on the day the 1% or a monthly penalty is added comes too late for
-- it, but one on the sixth day after the 1% day avoids the 4%, which is added
-- at that day's end (fork F4).
@ref s 139B(2)-(4), (7)
@export The late payment penalty accrued by a date under s 139B of the Tax Administration Act 1994 (NZ), if it applies (provisional tax, an earlier late payment within 2 years, or failing to pay after a notice of a further date): 1% of the unpaid tax the day after the default date, 4% of the tax to pay at the end of the 6th day after that, and — unless s 139B(2B) excludes it — 1% of the tax to pay each month after, each on the tax and penalties then unpaid. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Late payment facts`  @desc The unpaid tax, default date, payment date, the s 139B(1) facts, and whether incremental penalties are excluded
      asAt IS A DATE  @desc The day at which the penalty is measured
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the late payment penalty on` p `, as at` asAt MEANS
    IF   NOT `section 139B applies to` p
    THEN 0
    ELSE (`the tax to pay after` months `monthly penalties, starting from` afterInitial) MINUS u
    WHERE
        u MEANS p's `unpaid tax`
        d MEANS p's `default date`
        first MEANS `the day` 1 `days after` d
        GIVEN x IS A DATE
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        unpaidOn x MEANS
            x AT MOST asAt
            AND (CONSIDER p's `tax paid on`
                 WHEN JUST paid THEN paid AT LEAST x
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)
        afterOne MEANS IF unpaidOn first THEN u TIMES 1.01 ELSE u
        -- the 4% is added "at the end of the sixth day after" the 1% day, so
        -- a payment on that day comes in time.
        fourDay MEANS `the day` 7 `days after` d
        unpaidAtEnd MEANS
            fourDay AT MOST asAt
            AND (CONSIDER p's `tax paid on`
                 WHEN JUST paid THEN paid GREATER THAN fourDay
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)
        afterInitial MEANS IF unpaidAtEnd THEN afterOne TIMES 1.04 ELSE afterOne
        months MEANS
            IF   p's `incremental penalty excluded by s 139B(2B)`
            THEN 0
            ELSE `the number of monthly intervals from` first `while unpaid, up to` 600 `, unpaid on` unpaidOn

-- The number of whole monthly intervals, starting from a day, at the end of
-- each of which the tax is still unpaid (counting at most `limit`).
GIVEN start IS A DATE
      limit IS A NUMBER
      unpaid IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of monthly intervals from` start `while unpaid, up to` limit `, unpaid on` unpaid MEANS
    count 1
    WHERE
        GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        count k MEANS
            IF   k GREATER THAN limit OR NOT unpaid (`add months` start k)
            THEN k MINUS 1
            ELSE count (k PLUS 1)

GIVEN k IS A NUMBER, amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax to pay after` k `monthly penalties, starting from` amount MEANS
    IF k AT MOST 0 THEN amount ELSE `the tax to pay after` (k MINUS 1) `monthly penalties, starting from` (amount TIMES 1.01)

§ `Goal 4 — shortfall penalties`

-- s 141A(2) "The penalty payable for not taking reasonable care is 20% of the
-- resulting tax shortfall." s 141B "(1D) A taxpayer is liable to pay a
-- shortfall penalty if the taxpayer takes an unacceptable tax position in
-- relation to income tax ... and the tax shortfall arising from the
-- taxpayer's tax position is more than both— (a) $50,000: (b) 1% of the
-- taxpayer's total tax figure for the relevant return period"; the penalty is
-- 20% (threshold added after the independent pass). s
-- 141C(2) "The penalty payable for gross carelessness is 40%". s 141D "(3)
-- ... 100% of the resulting tax shortfall. (3B) ... reduced to 20% ... if—
-- [a promoted arrangement, shortfalls under $50,000, independent advice]". s
-- 141E(4) "... evasion or a similar act ... is 150%".
@ref ss 141A(2), 141B, 141C(2), 141D(3)-(3B), 141E(4)
GIVEN s IS A `Shortfall facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the shortfall penalty rate for` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s's `culpability`
    WHEN `s 141A not taking reasonable care` THEN 0.2
    WHEN `s 141B an unacceptable tax position` THEN
        IF       s's `the tax is income tax`
             AND s's `tax shortfall` GREATER THAN 50000
             AND s's `tax shortfall` GREATER THAN 0.01 TIMES s's `total tax figure for the return period`
        THEN 0.2
        ELSE 0
    WHEN `s 141C gross carelessness` THEN 0.4
    WHEN `s 141D an abusive tax position` THEN IF s's `the s 141D(3B) reduction to 20% applies` THEN 0.2 ELSE 1
    WHEN `s 141E evasion or a similar act` THEN 1.5

-- s 141G "(3) The level by which the shortfall penalty is reduced— (a) for
-- pre-notification disclosure is— (i) 100%, if the shortfall penalty is for
-- not taking reasonable care, for taking an unacceptable tax position, or for
-- an unacceptable interpretation; or (ii) 75%, if subparagraph (i) does not
-- apply: (b) for post-notification disclosure is 40%." s 141H "(1) A shortfall
-- penalty ... under section 141B or section 141D may be reduced if ... the
-- taxpayer makes adequate disclosure ... (2) The level ... is 75%." Where
-- both apply, the larger reduction is taken (fork F5).
@ref ss 141G(1), (3), 141H(1)-(2)
GIVEN s IS A `Shortfall facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the disclosure reduction for` s MEANS
    max voluntary adequate
    WHERE
        careless MEANS
               s's `culpability` EQUALS `s 141A not taking reasonable care`
            OR s's `culpability` EQUALS `s 141B an unacceptable tax position`
        voluntary MEANS
            CONSIDER s's `voluntary disclosure`
            WHEN `no voluntary disclosure` THEN 0
            WHEN `before notification of an audit or investigation` THEN IF careless THEN 1 ELSE 0.75
            WHEN `after notification but before the audit or investigation starts` THEN 0.4
        adequate MEANS
            IF       s's `adequate disclosure when the position was taken`
                 AND (   s's `culpability` EQUALS `s 141B an unacceptable tax position`
                      OR s's `culpability` EQUALS `s 141D an abusive tax position`)
            THEN 0.75
            ELSE 0

-- s 141I "(1) A shortfall penalty ... must be reduced if and to the extent
-- that the tax shortfall is temporary. (2) The level ... is 75% of the
-- penalty that applies to all or that part of the tax shortfall that is a
-- temporary tax shortfall." s 141J "(1) This section applies ... if— (a) the
-- taxpayer makes a voluntary disclosure; and (b) the shortfall penalty is
-- payable in respect of a temporary tax shortfall; and (c) the shortfall
-- penalty would be reduced under section 141G or 141H ... (2) The shortfall
-- penalty is reduced by— (a) 100%, if— (i) [reasonable care, unacceptable tax
-- position or interpretation]; and (ii) ... disclosed ... before notification
-- ...; or (b) 75%, if paragraph (a) does not apply." On the temporary part
-- s 141J replaces ss 141G-141I; on the rest ss 141G-141H apply (fork F5).
@ref ss 141I(1)-(2), 141J
GIVEN s IS A `Shortfall facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the shortfall penalty after the disclosure and temporary reductions for` s MEANS
    permanentPart TIMES (1 MINUS `the disclosure reduction for` s)
    PLUS temporaryPart TIMES (1 MINUS temporaryReduction)
    WHERE
        rate MEANS `the shortfall penalty rate for` s
        temporary MEANS min (s's `temporary part of the shortfall`) (s's `tax shortfall`)
        temporaryPart MEANS rate TIMES temporary
        permanentPart MEANS rate TIMES (s's `tax shortfall` MINUS temporary)
        careless MEANS
               s's `culpability` EQUALS `s 141A not taking reasonable care`
            OR s's `culpability` EQUALS `s 141B an unacceptable tax position`
        temporaryReduction MEANS
            IF   NOT (s's `voluntary disclosure` EQUALS `no voluntary disclosure`)
            THEN IF   careless AND s's `voluntary disclosure` EQUALS `before notification of an audit or investigation`
                 THEN 1
                 ELSE 0.75
            ELSE max 0.75 (`the disclosure reduction for` s)

-- s 141FB "(1) A shortfall penalty ... under section 141E is reduced, to 50%
-- ... if the taxpayer is not— (a) convicted of an offence that is a
-- disqualifying offence: (b) liable for another shortfall penalty that is a
-- disqualifying penalty ... (2) [likewise for] sections 141A to 141D". s 141K
-- "(1) A shortfall penalty ... may be increased ... if the taxpayer obstructs
-- the Commissioner ... (2) The level by which a shortfall penalty may be
-- increased for obstruction is 25%." s 141JAA "(1) Despite section 141J, a
-- shortfall penalty ... for not taking reasonable care, or for taking an
-- unacceptable tax position, may not be more than $50,000 if the taxpayer
-- voluntarily discloses the shortfall under section 141G, or the Commissioner
-- determines the shortfall, no later than the date that is the later of— (a)
-- the date that is 3 months after the due date of the return ...; and (b) the
-- date that follows the due date ... by the lesser of— (i) 1 return period;
-- and (ii) 6 months. (2) This section does not apply if section 141K
-- applies." Order: the disclosure and temporary reductions, then s 141FB,
-- then s 141K, then the cap (fork F6).
@ref ss 141A-141E, 141FB, 141G-141K, 141JAA
@export The shortfall penalty under ss 141A-141K of the Tax Administration Act 1994 (NZ): 20% of the shortfall for not taking reasonable care, or for an unacceptable income tax position where the shortfall exceeds both $50,000 and 1% of the total tax figure, 40% for gross carelessness, 100% for an abusive tax position (20% under s 141D(3B)), 150% for evasion; reduced for voluntary disclosure (100% or 75% before notification, 40% after) or adequate disclosure (75%), by 75% on a temporary shortfall (s 141J on a disclosed one), then halved for good previous behaviour (s 141FB), increased 25% for obstruction, and capped at $50,000 for early-resolved reasonable care and unacceptable tax position penalties (s 141JAA). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Shortfall facts`  @desc The shortfall, culpability, disclosures, the temporary part, previous behaviour, obstruction, and the dates for s 141JAA
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the shortfall penalty for` s MEANS
    IF   capped
    THEN min 50000 increased
    ELSE increased
    WHERE
        reduced MEANS `the shortfall penalty after the disclosure and temporary reductions for` s
        behaved MEANS IF s's `no disqualifying offence or penalty` THEN reduced TIMES 0.5 ELSE reduced
        increased MEANS IF s's `obstructed the Commissioner` THEN behaved TIMES 1.25 ELSE behaved
        due MEANS s's `due date of the return`
        limit MEANS
            IF   `add months` due 3 GREATER THAN `add months` due (min (s's `return period in months`) 6)
            THEN `add months` due 3
            ELSE `add months` due (min (s's `return period in months`) 6)
        capped MEANS
                (   s's `culpability` EQUALS `s 141A not taking reasonable care`
                 OR s's `culpability` EQUALS `s 141B an unacceptable tax position`)
            AND NOT s's `obstructed the Commissioner`
            AND s's `shortfall disclosed or determined on` AT MOST limit
